  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the maximum outcomes (2500 vs. 2400) — is considered by the individual, as they chose the lottery with the higher prize. The individual’s justification (choosing the higher prize due to similar probabilities) matches the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome when maximum outcomes differ. Although the individual does not explicitly mention the minimum outcome or the comparison of outcomes in detail, the core logic — selecting the lottery with the higher maximum payoff — is consistent with the decision reason. Therefore, the individual used the decision reason, even if implicitly or briefly stated.",
